From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:07:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: strong name signature verification and assembly
 tokens (3316)

DECISIONS-2 NET-HOST, CORE review: security. StrongNameSignatureVerification[Ex]
were stubs, the Ex one reporting every file as verified. They now implement the
ECMA-335 II.6.2 check: parse the PE/CLR headers, read the assembly's public key
through the metadata engine, hash the DOS header/stub, the PE headers (checksum
and certificate entry cleared), the section headers and every section except the
signature, and verify the RSA signature with CryptoAPI. Unsigned, delay-signed,
tampered, truncated or non-managed files are refused with the CORSEC_E_*
HRESULT in StrongNameErrorInfo. HKLM\Software\Microsoft\StrongName\Verification
entries (name,token / *,token / *,*) skip verification unless it is forced, and
then pfWasVerified is false. StrongNameTokenFromAssembly and the new
StrongNameTokenFromAssemblyEx return the token (and the public key) of the
assembly's metadata key.

